  <node unique_id="3" master_id="0" name="Setup Guide" prog_lang="custom-colors" tags="" readonly="0" nosearch_me="0" nosearch_ch="0" custom_icon_id="0" is_bold="0" foreground="" ts_creation="1791553256" ts_lastsave="1792000325">
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h1">SETUP GUIDE</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Team SchemaX | Student Information System</rich_text>
    <rich_text>


</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h2">1. INTRODUCTION</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
This guide explains how to prepare the development environment and open the SchemaX Student Information System project.
The application is developed using C# Windows Forms and MySQL. Visual Studio is used for development, while GitHub is used for version control and collaboration.


</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h2">2. SOFTWARE REQUIREMENTS</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">1. Operating System</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
• Windows 11

• Windows 10 may also be compatible, depending on the installed development tools.


</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">2. Development Environment</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
◇ Visual Studio 2026

◇ .NET 10 SDK

◇ .NET Desktop Development workload


</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">3. Database Software</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
◇ MySQL Server

◇ MySQL Workbench


</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">4. Version Control</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
◇ Git

◇ GitHub account


</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">5. Documentation</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
◇ CherryTree




</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h2">3. DOWNLOAD THE PROJECT</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Step 1:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> Open Visual Studio 2026.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Step 2:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> Select "Clone a repository."
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Step 3:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> Enter the GitHub repository URL:
</rich_text>
    <rich_text link="webs https://github.com/reynalynsaavedrasamar25/SchemaX-SIS.git">https://github.com/reynalynsaavedrasamar25/SchemaX-SIS.git</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Step 4:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> Choose a local folder where the repository will be saved.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Step 5:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> Click "Clone" and wait for the process to finish.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Step 6:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> Open the SchemaX.SIS solution in Visual Studio.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Note:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> Use the team's designated branch or approved version when testing the project.


</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h2">4. OPEN AND BUILD THE APPLICATION</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Step 1:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> Open the SchemaX.SIS solution.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Step 2:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> Wait for Visual Studio to load the project and restore its dependencies.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Step 3:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> Check Solution Explorer to confirm that the project files are available.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Step 4:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> Select Build → Build Solution or press Ctrl + Shift + B.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Step 5:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> Check the Error List and Output window for any build errors.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Step 6:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> Press F5 to run the application.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Expected Result:</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
The Student Information System window should open if the project builds and starts successfully.


</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h2">5. MYSQL DATABASE SETUP</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Assigned Developer:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> Reynalyn Samar
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Step 1:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> Install and open MySQL Server and MySQL Workbench.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Step 2:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> Ensure that the MySQL service is running.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Step 3:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> Open MySQL Workbench and connect to the local MySQL server.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Step 4:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> Create or import the database using the team's approved SQL script.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Step 5:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> Confirm that the required tables are available.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Step 6:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> Configure the application's database connection using the team's approved settings.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Step 7:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> Test whether the application can communicate with MySQL.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Database Name:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> Pending confirmation
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">SQL Script Location:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> Pending confirmation
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Connection Configuration:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> Pending confirmation
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Note:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> Do not include actual database passwords or other secret credentials in this documentation or GitHub repository.


</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h2">6. PROJECT FILES AND MODULES</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Form1.cs</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
◇ Contains application form logic and event handlers.

◇ Includes current input validation and selection warnings.


</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Form1.Designer.cs</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
◇ Contains the Windows Forms interface components and event connections.


</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Helpers/Validator.cs</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
◇ Validates student information and required input formats.


</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Helpers/ExceptionHandler.cs</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
◇ Handles exceptions and displays user-friendly error messages.


</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Helpers/ErrorLog.cs</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
◇ Records exception information in a local log file.


</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">logs/errors.txt</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
◇ Generated when errors are logged.

◇ Excluded from Git through </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">.gitignore</rich_text>
    <rich_text>.


</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Database and CRUD Modules</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
◇ Awaiting final integration and verification.




</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h2">7. BASIC TROUBLESHOOTING</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Problem: The project does not build.</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
Suggested checks:
◇ Confirm that the required .NET SDK is installed.

◇ Check the Visual Studio Error List.

◇ Restore missing project dependencies.


</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Problem: The application cannot connect to MySQL.</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
Suggested checks:
◇ Confirm that the MySQL service is running.

◇ Check the database connection settings.

◇ Verify that the database and required tables exist.


</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Problem: A validation warning appears.</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
Suggested checks:
◇ Confirm that required fields are not empty.

◇ Check the Student ID format.

◇ Review the entered student information.


</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Problem: An unexpected application error occurs.</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
Suggested checks:
◇ Read the displayed error message.

◇ Check the generated error log, if available.

◇ Report the issue to the assigned developer.




</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h2">8. SETUP VERIFICATION STATUS</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Visual Studio Project:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> Previously built and launched successfully.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Input Validation:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> Previously tested successfully.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Error Logging:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> Previously tested successfully.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">MySQL Integration:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> Pending final verification.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Complete CRUD Operations:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> Pending integration and testing.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Full Application Setup:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> Not yet verified on a clean computer.

</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Document Status:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> In Progress
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Project Version:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> 1.0
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Responsible Team:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> Team SchemaX
