  <node unique_id="4" master_id="0" name="App Walkthrough" prog_lang="custom-colors" tags="" readonly="0" nosearch_me="0" nosearch_ch="0" custom_icon_id="0" is_bold="0" foreground="" ts_creation="1791553353" ts_lastsave="1792000303">
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h1">APPLICATION WALKTHROUGH</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Team SchemaX | Student Information System</rich_text>
    <rich_text>


</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h2">1. APPLICATION OVERVIEW</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
The SchemaX Student Information System is a desktop application developed using C# Windows Forms and MySQL.
The application is designed to manage student records through a graphical user interface.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Current Development Status:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> In Progress
This walkthrough describes the existing interface, implemented validation checks, and features awaiting integration.


</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h2">2. MAIN APPLICATION INTERFACE</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
The current application interface contains the following components:
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Student Information Fields:</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
• Student ID

• Student Name

• Contact Number

• Program

• Gender

• Year Level


</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Action Buttons:</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
◇ Add

◇ Edit

◇ Delete


</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Additional Components:</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
◇ Search field

◇ DataGridView for displaying student records


</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Assigned UI Developer:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> Zedric Zuñiga


</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h2">3. ADD STUDENT — INPUT VALIDATION</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Assigned Developer:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> Princess Ida Camasis
The Add button currently validates the information entered by the user.

</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h3">3.1 Student ID Validation</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Required Format:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> YYYY-XXXXX
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Example:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> 2026-00001
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Validation Rules:</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
◇ Student ID cannot be empty.

◇ Student ID must follow the required format.


</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Expected Behavior:</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
The application displays a warning if the Student ID is missing or incorrectly formatted.

</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h3">3.2 Student Name Validation</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Validation Rules:</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
◇ Student Name cannot be empty.

◇ Only letters, spaces, hyphens, and apostrophes are accepted.


</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Expected Behavior:</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
Invalid names trigger a validation warning.

</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h3">3.3 Contact Number Validation</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Validation Rules:</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
◇ Contact number cannot be empty.

◇ Must contain 7–15 characters.

◇ Only numbers, spaces, hyphens, and plus signs are accepted.


</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Expected Behavior:</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
The application displays a warning when the contact number does not follow the required format.

</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h3">3.4 Program Validation</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Validation Rule:</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
◇ Program cannot be empty or contain only spaces.


</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Expected Behavior:</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
The application displays a warning if the Program field is missing.

</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h3">3.5 Gender Validation</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Validation Rules:</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
◇ A gender must be selected.

◇ The selected value must match an available ComboBox option.


</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Expected Behavior:</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
Missing or invalid selections trigger a warning.

</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h3">3.6 Year Level Validation</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Validation Rules:</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
◇ A year level must be selected.

◇ The selected value must match an available ComboBox option.


</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Expected Behavior:</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
Missing or invalid selections trigger a warning.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Current Status:</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
The six form-field validation checks were previously tested successfully.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Important:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> Passing validation does not currently confirm that a student record was saved. Database insertion still requires CRUD integration.


</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h2">4. EDIT STUDENT</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Assigned CRUD Developer:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> Mariane Nuarin
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Current Implemented Behavior:</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
◇ Clicking Edit without selecting a student displays a warning.


</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Expected Final Behavior:</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
◇ The user selects an existing student.

◇ The application loads the selected information.

◇ The user modifies the information.

◇ The updated record is saved to the database.


</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Status:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> Selection warning implemented; complete editing functionality pending integration.


</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h2">5. DELETE STUDENT</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Assigned CRUD Developer:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> Mariane Nuarin
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Current Implemented Behavior:</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
◇ Clicking Delete without selecting a student displays a warning.


</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Expected Final Behavior:</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
◇ The user selects a student.

◇ The application requests confirmation.

◇ The selected student record is deleted from the database.

◇ The displayed records are updated.


</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Status:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> Selection warning implemented; complete deletion functionality pending integration.


</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h2">6. VIEW AND SEARCH STUDENTS</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Assigned UI Developer:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> Zedric Zuñiga
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Expected Final Behavior:</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
◇ Student records are displayed in the DataGridView.

◇ Users can search for specific students.

◇ Displayed information reflects the database records.


</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Status:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> Interface available; database-backed display and search require final verification.


</rich_text>
